# Asset Lab working agreement

This repo generates engine-agnostic 3D assets with headless Blender. Cursor is the
orchestrator; Blender is a deterministic worker driven only through `tools/ag.py`.

Full agent manual (pitfalls, timing, QA quirks): `docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md`.

## Non-negotiables

- Never ask the user to open the Blender UI. The only manual step that exists is
  `python tools/bootstrap.py`, and only if `python tools/ag.py doctor` fails.
- Never invoke `blender.exe` directly. Everything goes through `tools/ag.py` so that
  every run produces a QA report.
- Never write geometry values straight into a generator to make one asset. Assets are
  described by a spec in `assets/specs/`; generators stay parametric and reusable.
- Never weaken a QA gate to make a run pass. If `max_triangles` is genuinely too low,
  say so and change it deliberately; do not delete checks or add fallbacks.
- Errors must stay loud. No try/except that swallows a failure, no silent defaults for
  missing spec fields.

## The loop

1. Write or edit `assets/specs/<id>.json`.
2. `python tools/ag.py generate <id>` (builds, QA-gates, exports `.glb`, re-imports it,
   then renders previews).
3. Read the report. Exit code 0 means every gate passed.
4. Look at the PNGs in `assets/out/previews/` with the image reader. Judge proportions,
   silhouette and material, not just the numbers.
5. Iterate on the spec. Only touch the generator when no parameter can express the change.

Exit codes: `0` pass, `1` a QA gate or build failed, `2` bad spec or missing toolchain.

## Adding a generator

1. Create `blender/generators/<family>_<name>.py` exposing `MATERIAL_SLOTS` and
   `build(spec) -> list[bpy.types.Object]`.
2. Register it in `blender/lib/registry.py`.
3. Parse `spec.params` into a frozen dataclass with the strict helpers from
   `blender/lib/spec.py`, and reject impossible dimensions with a message that states
   the actual numbers.
4. Prefer `BoxBuilder` and let boxes interpenetrate. Never leave coplanar faces on the
   outside of an asset; they z-fight in every engine.
5. Finish with `apply_bevel`, `shade_flat` and `unwrap` so the mesh that ships is the
   mesh that was measured.

## Conventions

- Meters, Z-up while authoring; the exporter converts to Y-up for glTF.
- Origin centred on the footprint with the base at Z=0.
- Modifiers are applied before export, so QA numbers describe the shipped file.
- Materials are plain Principled BSDF values; textures are not part of this pipeline yet.
